# Generated per machine by step 4 of the installer. Each one embeds THAT machine's
# public key, so committing them invites copying one to another machine - which would
# authorize the wrong machine on that NAS account. They are cheap to regenerate:
#   Setup-ResticBackup.ps1 -NasSetup      /      setup-restic-backup.sh --nas-setup
nas-provision-*.sh

# Superseded first drafts. Kept on disk for reference, no value in history.
reference/

# --- Defensive: none of this belongs in the repo, ever ---------------------------
# Credentials and per-machine state live in C:\ProgramData\restic (Windows) and
# /etc/restic (Linux), never beside the scripts. These patterns exist so that a
# careless copy into this folder cannot be committed by accident.
password
mqtt-password
config.json
settings.psd1*
settings.env*
id_ed25519*
*.pem
*.key
known_hosts
progress.json
last-run.json
history.jsonl
excludes.txt
excludes.txt.bak
*.log
*.migrated
